## TIẾNG ANH · 16:30–17:00 — Thứ Tư: Quyết định thiết kế

> *"The decision I want to explain is putting ownership checks inside the query instead of before it.*
> *The obvious way is: fetch the record, compare the owner ID to the user ID, then act. That works, but it has three problems. It's two round trips. There's a window between the check and the action. And when it fails you have to decide what to return — and if you return 403, you've just confirmed the record exists, which leaks information.*
> *So instead the ownership condition goes in the WHERE clause. Delete where ID matches and user ID matches. If nothing comes back, I return 404 — same response whether the record belongs to someone else or doesn't exist at all.*
> *The rule I follow is that the user ID always comes from the token, never from the request body. If the client can send a user ID, the client can choose who to be.*
> *I tested this by creating two accounts and trying to read, update, and delete each other's records. That's the OWASP number one API risk, and the only way to know you don't have it is to try it."*

**5 từ mới:**

| Từ / cụm | Nghĩa | Câu mẫu |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `round trip` | một lượt đi về | *It's two round trips.* |
| `window` (giữa hai thao tác) | khe hở thời gian | *There's a window between the check and the action.* |
| `confirm it exists` | xác nhận sự tồn tại | *You've just confirmed the record exists.* |
| `WHERE clause` | mệnh đề where | *The condition goes in the WHERE clause.* |
| `choose who to be` | tự chọn mình là ai | *The client can choose who to be.* |

